# Drafted by Gemini (R19 narrator), edited. Arrival lines for Maidenmist's places.

~ enter:mm_gate
| Fifteen-foot spears of cold iron vanish into the wet grey wool of the fog on either hand. Between two stone reapers, the bent gate hangs open with a rust-bitten groan.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_corpse_road
| Smooth cobbles slick with grease and rain run wide enough for a hearse between the leaning stones. The fog presses against your throats like wet linen, smelling of turned clay.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_sepulcher
| Seven paved paths climb through drifting blue-green wisps to a cracked, moss-furred tomb. Six empty iron sconces flank its colossal doors, cold and waiting in the mist.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_highborn_crypts
| Dark polished marble gleams under the leering snouts of rain-streaked gargoyles while bats wheel overhead. A single iron brazier holds a bed of dull red coals that barely warms the damp.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_crypt_below
| Frost bites at your knuckles as you step down among rows of heavy stone sarcophagi. High in the vaults, roosting bats shift and chitter above the smell of old dust.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_cremation_gardens
| Cold rain drums hard upon the red brick walks, washing past rows of clay urns and overflowing basins. Somewhere in the drench, an iron bell tolls a slow, sodden measure.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_potters_field
| Plain wooden stakes lean over sunken, nameless sod while wet crows mutter in the mire. Pale amber lanterns drift low through the fog without a hand to carry them.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_mausoleum_lanes
| Ivy-choked vaults rise out of the bog like a sunken town, their cracked stones weeping black water. Every step sucks at your boots and sends up a sharp, sour stench of rot.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_burial_mounds
| Great grassy barrows swell from the mire, crowned by twisted trees with solemn faces grown into their bark. Boughs shaped like crooked fingers offer up apples way too red and sweet for a graveyard.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_shadestone_sanctuary
| Tall standing stones scored deep with orcish names ring a low ziggurat where an azure flame burns clear. Here the wind falls hush, holding a clean, cold stillness the rest of the graveyard has forgotten.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_kings_rest
| Before a palatial barrow rises the colossus of an armored king, his stone blade thrust into the boiling mist. Steel rings and dead men shout at its doors, fighting a war that never heard it ended.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_balefire_chamber
| Six iron sconces line this sixty-foot hall of fitted stone, waiting for their differently colored flames. At the far end, a tumbled choke of rubble leaks a slow, freezing draft of grey mist.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_undercroft
| Thousands of yellowing skulls stare from the packed dirt walls while pale mist pools around your ankles. A low shudder runs through the earthen floor, rattling dry teeth in their sockets.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_necropolis_depths
| Great gouges of torn rock mark where something huge clawed this cavern wide, leaving trails of pale green slime. Half-eaten dead folk jut from burrows in the muck, lit by a sickly, dripping glow.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_tomb
| Three-pronged iron platforms hang on massive chains over a pit lit by cold blue-green balefire. Above them, the very air splits open like frayed cloth, bleeding freezing mist and a sound like weeping wind.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_gravestones_a
| Rolling hills of crowded headstones tilt into the fog, packed so close your cloaks brush the wet lichen. Out between the rows, boots shuffle through the dead grass, always a few paces out of sight.
cooldown 0

~ enter:mm_gravestones_b
| Crooked markers crowd shoulder to shoulder across the sodden hills as far as the mist allows. Something heavy keeps pace with you behind the stones, stopping whenever you stop to listen.
cooldown 0
